  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I checked your quarantine. The scanned document email (\"Scanned document 0931.zip\" from scanner@docs-share.example) has been flagged by our security filter as malware, and I'm not able to release it. Please don't open the zip file or click anything in that email. I've passed it to our Tier 2 team so they can review it and confirm whether it's safe. If you're expecting copier scans, please contact the copier's support or the person who set up the scan-to-email service so they can confirm the correct sending address. Also, your account is currently showing as locked after several failed sign-in attempts. If you need access restored, let us know and we'll follow up.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (user_id 4, Tom Becker, Finance, usual hours 09:00-17:00 ET, device BL-LT-0104). Account status is locked with 5 failed logins; sign_in not blocked; password last set 2026-07-23. Not raised by the user, so no unlock requested. Quarantine check shows two messages: Q-1004 (billing@harborview-supplies.example, Invoice #4471, reason spam, releasable) which the user did not ask for, and Q-1005 (scanner@docs-share.example, Scanned document 0931.zip, received 2026-10-09, reason malware, NOT releasable). The user's request is for Q-1005. Per KB-008 and KB-007, malware-flagged mail is never released and the sender/content needs a person to review. Did not call release_email. Escalated to Tier 2 to review the docs-share.example sender and the zip, confirm whether the copier scan workflow uses that address, and decide on the account lockout. Suggest checking whether any other users received mail from scanner@docs-share.example. The user did not report clicking or entering credentials, so no KB-029 steps were triggered; Tier 2 should confirm this with the user.",
